2.3 Performance Requirements

The application must be designed as an Enterprise-Level High-Traffic Food Delivery Platform, similar in architecture and scalability to Foodpanda or Uber Eats.

Expected Traffic

Daily Orders

2,000–5,000+

Concurrent Users

1,000+

Peak Time

Lunch

Dinner

Weekend

Festival

The application must support thousands of users placing orders simultaneously without noticeable performance degradation.

Performance Goals

Page Load

Less than 2 seconds

API Response

Less than 300 milliseconds (average)

Database Queries

Optimized with indexes.

Caching

Redis Cache.

Image Loading

Lazy Loading

WebP Format

Compression

CDN Ready

Scalability

The system must support horizontal scaling.

Additional servers should be deployable without modifying application logic.

The architecture must support future migration to Kubernetes or cloud-native infrastructure if required.

SEO Requirements

